    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Growing our Membership Base Demonstrating the Power of Inclusive Business for the SDGs 1. By Dec 2020, increase BCtA membership base to 300 companies with high quality, innovative, scalable IB commitments (cumulative target) and 270 by June 2020. 2. Continue to build a strong pipeline of potential member companies and encourage them to consider IB models. 3. By Dec 2020, reach at least 170 companies through online and offline capacity building on the SDG/IB Maturity Tool and management practices (and 150 by June 2020). BCtA&#x2019;s country level work 1. Continue to carry out capacity building activities and deploy BCtA tools and services including SDG/IB Maturity Tool and Impact Measurement Tool in Colombia and Bangladesh. 2. Encourage increased quality in private sector engagement in SDGs through inclusive business, growing BCtA membership by 12 by Dec 2020. 3. Continued engagement on IB and SDGs through knowledge products and advocacy through the delivery of training to 55 companies by Dec 2020; assess opportunities for further engagement through UNDP private sector events and network, provide relevant policy inputs through IB knowledge products. 4. Roll out our tools and services in Tunisia through key stakeholders and strategic partners, and thereby grow our membership base in the country. Building capacity of BCtA Member Companies and Inclusive Business to Measure and Manage Impact 1. 155 companies provided with online and in-person capacity building on impact management 2. At least 60% of member companies share annual progress report in June and Dec 2020. 3. Collaborate with key players in the SDG measurement space to further advance BCtA&#x2019;s methodology and approach. Knowledge management and communication in 2019 1. Position BCtA Secretariat and its member companies as active thought leaders in the field of inclusive business through regular publication and distribution of quality content that addresses leading issues related to IB (5 document cases). 2. Maintain BCtA website as the go-to platform for the latest development and knowledge on IB, with a focus on promoting its range of tool-kits for IB. 3. Continue growing social media audience following and interaction across BCtA accounts to support Objective 2 (above) and reach and engage diverse and strategic online audiences. 4. Advance BCtA knowledge management systems to efficiently capture the explicit and tacit knowledge produced by BCtA, its members, partners and relevant stakeholders, and ensure the strategic use of this knowledge to catalyze learning and evidence.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
    </period>
